  "title": "〜た — casual “did”",
  "pattern": "the て form, with た for て: {行|い}った, {食|た}べた, した",
  "explanation": "The casual past is the て form with た instead of て: {行|い}って → {行|い}った, {食|た}べて → {食|た}べた, して → した. So if you know a verb’s て form, which every verb card shows, you know its past. “Didn’t” turns ない into なかった: {行|い}かなかった.",
  "natural": "Telling a friend about your day: {昨日|きのう}、{友達|ともだち}に{会|あ}った. い-adjectives have their own past: {楽|たの}しかった.",
  "stiff": "With staff, strangers and a partner’s parents, use ました instead: {行|い}きました.",
